    "answer": {
      "short": "Mary is correct. The $y$-axis is not the graph of a function because $x=0$ has multiple $y$-values.",
      "worked": "Mary is correct. Every point on the $y$-axis has $x=0$, so this single input corresponds to multiple $y$-values. A function must assign exactly one output to each input in its domain. Therefore, despite its $180^\\circ$ rotational symmetry, the $y$-axis cannot represent an odd function.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
